Changes made by Epinoia Horizon include, without limitation:

  * Rebranding: product name, copy, documentation, and documentation site.
  * A new visual identity: the wizard-hat app icon, rune/arcane glyph
    replacements for the upstream caduceus marks, and the gold/navy palette.
  * A vendored UI design system packaged as @merlin/ui.
  * Desktop packaging, installer, and update-channel changes for the Merlin
    distribution.
  * Atlas Portal, a hosted model and tool gateway, with its own transport and
    rate guard (agent/atlas_wire.py, agent/atlas_rate_guard.py).
  * Desktop runtime hardening in the Electron application: backend discovery
    and exit recovery, host attach and spawn gating, pool limits and
    reclamation.
  * Policy seal: an optional governance mode in agent/prompt_builder.py that
    keeps memory and skill tools dormant unless explicitly invoked.
  * Feature work landed after the fork point.

